    <section class="s rv" id="summary">
      <span class="eyebrow">The one-liner</span>
      <h2><span class="num">01</span>Summary</h2>
      <p class="lead">$CLEAN is built on one sticky joke — <strong>clean hands, dirty money</strong> — wrapped around a staking app with <strong>no fees</strong> and a burn loop that rewards conviction.</p>
      <p>You "wash" your bags by staking into spin cycles, and you make them rarer by <strong>burning</strong> $CLEAN to boost your yield. Every burn is permanent and shrinks supply for everyone. There is no tax, no unstake fee, and no treasury skim — the only thing "clean" about crypto.</p>
      <div class="panel accent"><strong>Thesis in a sentence:</strong> a meme on the outside, unusually trustworthy on the inside — and that contrast is the whole story.</div>
    </section>

    <section class="s rv" id="problem">
      <span class="eyebrow">The problem</span>
      <h2><span class="num">02</span>Why most meme coins die</h2>
      <p>Three reasons, every time:</p>
      <ul class="clean">
        <li><strong>No reason to hold</strong> past the first candle.</li>
        <li><strong>Extractive tokenomics</strong> — team wallets and transfer taxes quietly draining holders.</li>
        <li><strong>A brand that can't outlive the meme</strong> once the timeline moves on.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>CLEAN answers each: a staking + burn loop gives a reason to hold; <strong>zero fees</strong> means nothing is extracted; and "clean hands, dirty money" is an ownable visual identity (gloves, sparkle, the laundry metaphor) that extends straight into apparel and physical products.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s rv" id="mechanics">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h2><span class="num">03</span>Mechanics</h2>

      <h3>Soft staking — your keys, your coins</h3>
      <p>There are <strong>no lock-ups and no deposits</strong>. You "enroll" the $CLEAN already
      sitting in your own wallet; tokens <strong>never leave your custody</strong>. Yield accrues
      every second on what you still hold — sell, and you simply stop earning on what you sold.</p>
      <p>Your rate is one transparent formula, computed identically in the app, this page, and the
      API (numbers below are <strong>live from the protocol</strong>):</p>
      <div class="quote">effective APR = <b><span data-econ="base_pct">40%</span> base</b> × (1 + amount + loyalty + referral) + burn bonus</div>
      <div class="wraptbl"><table class="tbl">
        <tr><th>Booster</th><th>How</th><th>Adds</th><th>Cap</th></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Amount</b></td><td>hold ≥ <span data-econ="tier2_at">100K</span> / <span data-econ="tier1_at">1M</span> / <span data-econ="tier0_at">10M</span></td><td>+<span data-econ="tier2_pct">10%</span> / +<span data-econ="tier1_pct">25%</span> / +<span data-econ="tier0_pct">50%</span></td><td>highest tier</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Loyalty</b></td><td>every 30 days staked</td><td>+<span data-econ="loyalty_pct">5%</span></td><td>+<span data-econ="loyalty_cap_pct">50%</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Referrals</b></td><td>each friend who stakes</td><td>+<span data-econ="ref_pct">2%</span></td><td>+<span data-econ="ref_cap_pct">30%</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>🔥 Burn</b></td><td>per <span data-econ="burn_unit">100K</span> burned (permanent)</td><td>+<span data-econ="burn_per_pct">5%</span> APR</td><td>+<span data-econ="burn_cap_pct">200%</span> APR</td></tr>
      </table></div>
      <p style="font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted)">Multipliers stack on the base; the burn bonus adds flat APR on top. Fully boosted: ~<span data-econ="max_apr_pct_t">292</span>% — funded from the project treasury and never guaranteed.</p>

      <h3>Burn-to-Boost — the core loop</h3>
      <p>Instead of a fee, the only way to amplify yield is to <strong>burn $CLEAN</strong>. Burning permanently destroys tokens and raises your personal APR by up to <strong>+<span data-econ="burn_cap_pct2">200%</span></strong>. Every burn is verified <strong>on-chain</strong> (finalized) before it is credited — once, ever, per transaction.</p>
      <div class="loop">
        <span class="node">Stake</span><span class="arr">→</span>
        <span class="node fire">🔥 Burn $CLEAN</span><span class="arr">→</span>
        <span class="node">APR ↑ (+<span data-econ="burn_cap_pct3">200%</span>)</span><span class="arr">→</span>
        <span class="node">Supply ↓</span><span class="arr">→</span>
        <span class="node">Scarcity ↑</span>
      </div>
      <div class="quote">The holder who wants more yield pays for it by making everyone else's tokens rarer. That's "dirty money gets clean" — on-chain.</div>

      <h3>No fees</h3>
      <p>No deposit fee, no unstake fee, no transfer tax. The only cost is Solana network gas, paid to validators — never to us. "Clean" is the product promise <em>and</em> the fee schedule.</p>

      <h3>Merch — the real-world surface</h3>
      <p>A first-class storefront sells tees and hoodies, plus — on-brand — actual nitrile gloves and cleaning wipes. Merch is real revenue independent of price, free advertising (people wearing the meme), and a bridge to non-crypto audiences.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s rv" id="tokenomics">
      <span class="eyebrow">The numbers</span>
      <h2><span class="num">04</span>Tokenomics</h2>
      <p>Fixed max supply: <strong>1,000,000,000 $CLEAN</strong>, fair-launched on pump.fun —
      <strong>no presale, no team allocation, no fee switch</strong>. The only thing that ever
      changes supply is the burn loop, and it only goes down.</p>
      <div class="cstats" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(130px,1fr));gap:12px;margin:18px 0">
        <div class="cstat"><div class="k"><span data-stat="staked">—</span></div><div class="l">$CLEAN staked · live</div></div>
        <div class="cstat"><div class="k"><span data-stat="stakers">—</span></div><div class="l">Active stakers · live</div></div>
        <div class="cstat"><div class="k"><span data-stat="total_burned">—</span></div><div class="l">$CLEAN burned · live</div></div>
        <div class="cstat"><div class="k"><span data-stat="burners">—</span></div><div class="l">Burners · live</div></div>
      </div>
      <h3>Emissions &amp; sustainability</h3>
      <p>Staking rewards are funded from the <strong>project treasury</strong> and paid out manually — no hot wallet ever lives on a server. Rates are config, not promises: they can taper as participation grows, and that is disclosed up front. Long-term value rests on burn-driven scarcity and brand demand, not perpetual high APR.</p>
      <h3>Deflation accounting</h3>
      <p>Every burn is on-chain and verifiable. A public <strong>burn counter</strong> (total burned, % of supply removed) is displayed in-app and becomes a core marketing artifact.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s rv" id="architecture">
      <span class="eyebrow">Under the hood</span>
      <h2><span class="num">05</span>Architecture</h2>
      <ul class="clean">
        <li><strong>Chain:</strong> Solana — fast, cheap, meme-native liquidity.</li>
        <li><strong>Token:</strong> SPL mint; authorities renounced post-setup where possible.</li>
        <li><strong>Staking:</strong> non-custodial "soft staking" — balances are read from chain; nothing is ever deposited. Login is an ed25519 wallet signature over a single-use nonce.</li>
        <li><strong>Burns:</strong> verified against the finalized on-chain transaction (mint + authority checked) before any boost is credited — each tx credited exactly once.</li>
        <li><strong>Accounting:</strong> integer base units, append-only ledger, automated daily reconciliation — every reward is auditable.</li>
        <li><strong>App:</strong> a single-file front end integrating through a documented adapter (CONFIG + API).</li>
        <li><strong>Commerce:</strong> Shopify or Crossmint for fulfilment; pay by card, SOL, or $CLEAN.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s rv" id="security">
      <span class="eyebrow">Trust is the brand</span>
      <h2><span class="num">06</span>Security &amp; trust</h2>
      <p>Three internal forensic audits of the money path (atomic claims, burn idempotency, anti-inflation accrual) with the reports published in the repo, plus a continuous regression suite. Treasury payouts are manual from a multisig — no private key on any server. Verifiable burns. Clear, repeated "meme, not an investment" disclaimers. With CLEAN, one extractive or dishonest move would break the entire thesis — so it won't be made.</p>
